// TEST: Symmetric Literal With A Rectangular Row (rejects)
// ERROR: BL3007
// ERROR-CONTAINS: but the simplex row there is 2 wide
// The rectangular nest — the shape a reader who thinks of SymIdx<2,3> as a
// 3x3 matrix writes. Row 1 of the simplex holds the cells (1,1) and (1,2);
// a third entry there names (1,3), which is off the axis. The diagnostic must
// point at the offending ROW, not at the row after it: the walk stops at the
// first bad cell precisely so the span survives.
let A: Array<Int64 like SymIdx<2, 3>> = [
    [1, 2, 3],
    [4, 5, 6],
    [7]
]
